---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = [



  {
    q: 'What is the best free Word Counter?',
    a: 'RealWordCounter is widely considered the best free word counter online. It offers live word count, character count, goal tracker, readability score, platform limits checker, and UPSC/CBSE exam presets — all in one place, with no sign-up required and 100% private in-browser processing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can ChatGPT do word count?',
    a: 'ChatGPT can estimate word count when you paste text into it, but it is not always precise and does not offer real-time counting, goal tracking, or character-level analysis. A dedicated tool like RealWordCounter gives you instant, accurate counts as you type — without uploading your text to any external AI service.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long is a 700 word talk?',
    a: 'A 700-word talk takes approximately 4 to 5 minutes at an average speaking pace of 130–150 words per minute. At a slow, deliberate pace (100 wpm) it runs about 7 minutes; at a fast pace (180 wpm) it comes in around 4 minutes. Use RealWordCounter\'s speaking time estimate to plan your talk length accurately.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I count words online for free?',
    a: 'To count words online for free, open RealWordCounter.com, paste or type your text into the editor, and the word count updates instantly as you type. No sign-up, no payment, and no data is ever sent to a server. You can also upload .txt, .docx, .pdf, or .md files directly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I speak 1000 words in 5 minutes?',
    a: 'Speaking 1000 words in 5 minutes requires a pace of 200 words per minute, which is on the faster end of natural speech. Most people speak at 130–150 wpm, making 1000 words a 6–7 minute delivery at a comfortable pace. RealWordCounter displays your estimated speaking time automatically as you write.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many pages is 300 word count?',
    a: '300 words is approximately half a page when typed in 12-point font with double spacing (the common academic format). In single spacing it is roughly a quarter of a page. The exact length varies depending on font size, margins, and line spacing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which app can count words?',
    a: 'Microsoft Word, Google Docs, and Apple Pages all have built-in word counters. For a dedicated, free, and privacy-focused option that requires no app install, RealWordCounter.com works directly in any browser on any device — including mobile — and also shows character count, readability, and platform limits.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does Google Docs have a word counter?',
    a: 'Yes. Google Docs has a built-in word counter. Go to Tools → Word count (or press Ctrl+Shift+C on Windows / Cmd+Shift+C on Mac) to see word count, character count, and page count. You can also enable "Display word count while typing" for a live counter. For additional metrics like readability and keyword density, use RealWordCounter alongside Google Docs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does Microsoft Word have a word counter?',
    a: 'Yes. Microsoft Word displays the word count in the status bar at the bottom of every document. For more detail — including characters, paragraphs, and lines — go to Review → Word Count. The count updates automatically as you type.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which word would best introduce a counter claim?',
    a: 'Words that best introduce a counter claim include: "However," "On the other hand," "Nevertheless," "Admittedly," "Although," "Despite this," and "Critics argue that." These transition words signal to the reader that you are acknowledging an opposing viewpoint before refuting or qualifying it in your argument.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the best free online word counter tool?',
    a: 'RealWordCounter.com is the best free online word counter tool available today. It combines live word count, character count, reading and speaking time, keyword density, readability score (Flesch), platform limits checker, word goal tracker, and exam presets for UPSC and CBSE — all completely free, with no sign-up and full in-browser privacy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How to word a counter offer?',
    a: 'To word a counter offer effectively: (1) Thank the other party for their offer to set a positive tone. (2) Reference the specific terms you are countering. (3) State your position clearly with a specific number or condition. (4) Briefly justify it with relevant experience, market data, or value you bring. (5) Invite further discussion and express willingness to reach an agreement.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How to word a counter offer for salary?',
    a: 'To word a salary counter offer professionally: start by expressing genuine enthusiasm for the role, then acknowledge the offer and state a specific higher figure based on your research or experience. For example: "I\'m very excited about this opportunity. Based on my experience and current market rates, I was expecting a salary closer to ₹X. Is there flexibility there?" Keep the tone collaborative, not adversarial.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the word counter mean?',
    a: 'The word "counter" in "word counter" means a tool that counts — specifically one that tallies the number of individual words in a given piece of text. A word counter helps writers, students, and professionals measure text length, meet word limits for exams or platforms, and track writing progress toward a target.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which Indian exams are supported?',
    a: 'RealWordCounter has built-in presets for UPSC Mains (150 words for 10-mark answers, 250 words for 15-mark answers, 1100 words for essays), CBSE (500 words), and IELTS Task 1 and Task 2.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use this offline?',
    a: 'Yes. Once the page has loaded, the word counter and all analysis tools work without an internet connection. Your draft is saved to your browser using localStorage.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it support Hindi and other Indian languages?',
    a: 'Character count and paragraph count work for Hindi and any Unicode language. Word count works best with space-separated words. For Hindi, the character count is most useful for exam preparation.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="RealWordCounter — Free Word Counter, Goal Tracker and Writing Tools"
  description="Free online word counter with goal tracker, platform limits checker, readability score, and exam presets for UPSC, CBSE and IELTS. 100% private — no signup required."
  canonical="https://realwordcounter.com/"
  faqSchema={faqSchema}
  keywords="word counter, word counter free, word counter online, word counter tool, free word counter, online word counter, word counter google docs, word counter website, text word counter, essay word counter"
  ogImage="og-home.png"
>

  <!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="hero-eyebrow">
          <span class="badge badge-primary">Free for Indian students &amp; writers</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="hero-heading">
          Free Writing Tools That Help You Write Better
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-sub">
          The free word counter online tool for students and creators. Track word goals,
          prep for UPSC &amp; CBSE exams, check platform limits, and write with full
          privacy — no sign-up, no data stored, works offline.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-cta-row">
          <a href="/word-counter" class="btn btn-primary btn-pill">Start Writing →</a>
          <a href="#tools" class="btn btn-secondary btn-pill">Explore Tools</a>
        </div>

        <div class="trust-badges">
          <span class="trust-badge">✓ No Signup</span>
          <span class="trust-badge">✓ No Data Stored</span>
          <span class="trust-badge">✓ Works Offline</span>
          <span class="trust-badge trust-badge-green">🔒 100% Private</span>
        </div>

        <nav class="hero-page-links" aria-label="Quick links">
          <a href="/about">About Us</a>
          <span class="hero-page-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
          <span class="hero-page-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>
          <span class="hero-page-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="hero-card-mockup">
          <div class="mockup-row">
            <div class="mockup-stat"><span class="mockup-num">1,247</span><span class="mockup-lbl">Words</span></div>
            <div class="mockup-stat"><span class="mockup-num">6,843</span><span class="mockup-lbl">Characters</span></div>
            <div class="mockup-stat"><span class="mockup-num">6 min</span><span class="mockup-lbl">Reading Time</span></div>
            <div class="mockup-stat"><span class="mockup-num">248</span><span class="mockup-lbl">Unique Words</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mockup-goal">
            <div class="mockup-goal-label">Goal: 1500 words — 83% complete</div>
            <div class="mockup-bar"><div class="mockup-bar-fill" style="width:83%"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mockup-presets">
            <span class="mockup-preset active">UPSC 150</span>
            <span class="mockup-preset">CBSE 500</span>
            <span class="mockup-preset">IELTS Task 2</span>
            <span class="mockup-preset">Blog 1500</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Tools directory ───────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section tools-section" id="tools">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Tools</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Everything a writer needs</h2>
      <p class="section-subtext">Purpose-built for Indian students, bloggers, and content creators.</p>

      <div class="tools-grid">

        <a href="/word-counter" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">📝</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Word Counter</h3>
            <p>Live word count, character count, goal tracker, readability score, platform limits, file upload, case converter, keyword density, and export.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Goal Tracker</span><span>Platform Limits</span><span>File Upload</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/upsc-word-counter" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">🏛️</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>UPSC Word Counter</h3>
            <p>Pre-loaded with GS 150 and 250-word limits, essay presets, and a full UPSC reference table with Set Goal buttons.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>UPSC Presets</span><span>GS Reference</span><span>Essay Mode</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/character-counter" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">🔢</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Character Counter</h3>
            <p>Character-focused counter with all 10 platform limits as the hero feature. File upload, export, and autosave included.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Platform Limits</span><span>File Upload</span><span>Export</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/twitter-character-counter" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">🐦</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Twitter Counter</h3>
            <p>Live tweet preview with overflow highlighted in red. Color-coded counter turns amber at 240 and red over 280 characters.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Tweet Preview</span><span>Overflow Highlight</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/instagram-caption-checker" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">📸</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Instagram Checker</h3>
            <p>Caption mode (2200 chars) and bio mode (150 chars). Counts hashtags (max 30), emoji, and shows an Instagram feed preview.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Caption/Bio Toggle</span><span>Hashtag Counter</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/meta-description-checker" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">🔍</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Meta Description Checker</h3>
            <p>Live Google SERP preview with title (60 chars) and description (155 chars) inputs. SEO checklist with pass/fail criteria.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Google Preview</span><span>SEO Checklist</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/text-case-converter" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">✏️</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Text Case Converter</h3>
            <p>Eight transformations: UPPERCASE, lowercase, Title Case, Sentence case, Alternating, Remove Spaces, Reverse Text, Reverse Words. Undo up to 10 steps.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>8 Transforms</span><span>Undo History</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/readability-checker" class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-card-icon">📖</div>
          <div class="tool-card-body">
            <h3>Readability Checker</h3>
            <p>Flesch Reading Ease score with visual gauge, sentence length breakdown, syllable analysis, and dynamic improvement suggestions.</p>
            <div class="tool-card-features"><span>Flesch Score</span><span>Score Gauge</span><span>Suggestions</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="tool-card-cta">Open tool →</span>
        </a>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Why RealWordCounter ───────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section why-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Why us</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Built to beat the competition</h2>
      <p class="section-subtext">Every feature here is missing from wordcounter.net, countwordsfree.com, and toolninja.in.</p>

      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-icon">🎯</div>
          <h4>Word Goal Tracker</h4>
          <p>Set a target and watch a live progress bar fill as you write. Presets for UPSC 150, UPSC 250, CBSE 500, IELTS Task 1 &amp; 2, Blog, and LinkedIn built in. No competitor has this.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-icon">📱</div>
          <h4>Platform Limits Checker</h4>
          <p>See instantly if your text fits Twitter, Instagram, LinkedIn, Meta Description, YouTube, and 6 more platforms — all updating live as you type.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-icon">💾</div>
          <h4>Autosave — Never Lose Work</h4>
          <p>Your draft is saved to your browser every second you type. Refresh the page and your text comes right back. No account needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-icon">🔒</div>
          <h4>100% Private — Zero Tracking</h4>
          <p>Text never leaves your device. All computation happens in JavaScript in your browser. No login, no cookies for tracking, no server uploads. Ever.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Privacy section ───────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section privacy-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="privacy-card">
        <div class="privacy-icon">🔒</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Your privacy is not negotiable</h2>
          <p>
            Every analysis — word count, readability, keyword density — happens in your
            browser using JavaScript. Your text is never uploaded anywhere.
            We never see it. There is no server, no database, no account.
            RealWordCounter works fully offline after the first load.
            The only thing stored is your own draft in your own browser's localStorage,
            accessible only by you.
          </p>
          <div class="privacy-badges">
            <span class="trust-badge trust-badge-green">🔒 No server uploads</span>
            <span class="trust-badge trust-badge-green">🔒 No cookies</span>
            <span class="trust-badge trust-badge-green">🔒 No account required</span>
            <span class="trust-badge trust-badge-green">🔒 Works offline</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── FAQ ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section faq-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqSchema.map(({ q, a }) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{q}</summary>
            <div class="details-body">{a}</div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Company links ────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section company-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">About</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Get to know RealWordCounter</h2>
      <p class="section-subtext">Built for Indian students and writers. Free forever. 100% private.</p>

      <div class="company-grid">
        <a href="/about" class="company-card">
          <div class="company-card-icon">👋</div>
          <div>
            <h3>About Us</h3>
            <p>Learn why we built RealWordCounter and who we're building it for.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="company-card-cta">Read more →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="company-card">
          <div class="company-card-icon">✉️</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Contact Us</h3>
            <p>Found a bug or have a feature idea? We reply within 48 hours on weekdays.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="company-card-cta">Get in touch →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/privacy-policy" class="company-card">
          <div class="company-card-icon">🔒</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Privacy Policy</h3>
            <p>We never store your text. See exactly what data we do and don't collect.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="company-card-cta">Read policy →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/terms" class="company-card">
          <div class="company-card-icon">📄</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Terms &amp; Conditions</h3>
            <p>The rules that govern your use of the site — short and plain-English.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="company-card-cta">Read terms →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── SEO Article ───────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section seo-article-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="seo-article">
        <h2>What Is a Word Counter and Why Do You Need One?</h2>

        <p>
          A <strong>word counter</strong> is a tool that counts the number of words in a piece
          of text — instantly and accurately. Whether you are writing an essay, a blog post,
          a social media caption, or an exam answer, knowing your word count is essential.
          RealWordCounter is a <strong>free word counter online</strong> that goes far beyond
          a simple number: it gives you live word count, character count, readability scores,
          keyword density, and more — all in one place.
        </p>

        <h3>Why Use a Free Word Counter Online?</h3>

        <p>
          Word processors like Microsoft Word and Google Docs do have built-in word count
          features. But a dedicated <strong>free word counter</strong> offers clear advantages
          over them. Unlike the <strong>word counter in Google Docs</strong>, RealWordCounter
          works directly in your browser on any device — without needing a Google account,
          an active document, or any software installed. Just open the page, paste your text,
          and get instant results. It is faster, lighter, and continues to work offline after
          the first page load.
        </p>

        <p>
          A standalone <strong>word counter tool</strong> also gives you far more than a single
          number. Our <strong>online word counter</strong> displays word count, character count
          (with and without spaces), sentence count, paragraph count, estimated reading time,
          speaking time, and the number of unique words — all updating live as you type. No
          other <strong>word counter website</strong> in India offers this combination of
          features completely free, with zero tracking and no login required.
        </p>

        <h3>Features That Make RealWordCounter the Best Word Counter Tool</h3>

        <p>
          Most <strong>text word counter</strong> websites show one number and stop there.
          RealWordCounter is built differently. Here is what sets it apart:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Word Goal Tracker</strong> — Set a target and watch a live progress bar fill
            as you write. Presets include UPSC 150, UPSC 250, UPSC Essay 1100, CBSE 500,
            IELTS Task 1 &amp; 2, Blog 1500, and LinkedIn 300. No competitor has this.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Platform Limits Checker</strong> — See instantly whether your text fits
            Twitter/X (280 characters), Instagram post (2,200 characters), LinkedIn post
            (3,000 characters), Meta description (155 characters), YouTube title, SMS, and more.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Readability Score</strong> — Get a Flesch Reading Ease score with a grade-level
            label so you always know if your text is easy, standard, or difficult to read.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keyword Density</strong> — The top 10 non-stop keywords appear with frequency
            bars, making it easy to check on-page SEO without leaving the editor.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>File Import</strong> — Upload .txt, .docx, .pdf, or .md files and count
            words without manual copy-pasting.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Autosave</strong> — Your draft is saved automatically to your browser every
            second you type, so you never lose work if you close the tab.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Who Uses This Online Word Counter?</h3>

        <p>
          Our <strong>word counter free</strong> tool is used by a wide range of writers every day:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>UPSC aspirants</strong> practising answer writing within the 150-word and
            250-word limits for General Studies papers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Students</strong> completing CBSE assignments, IELTS essays, and college
            application essays that have strict word limits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Bloggers and content creators</strong> hitting target lengths for SEO articles
            and social media posts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Journalists and editors</strong> submitting pieces with publisher-mandated
            word counts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Social media managers</strong> keeping LinkedIn posts, Instagram captions,
            and tweets within platform character limits.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>100% Private — Your Text Never Leaves Your Device</h3>

        <p>
          Unlike many word counter websites that send your text to a server for processing,
          RealWordCounter analyses everything locally in your browser using JavaScript. Your
          text is never uploaded anywhere — not even to our servers. The tool works completely
          offline after the first page load, and the only thing stored is your own draft in your
          own browser's localStorage, accessible only by you.
        </p>

        <p>
          Whether you need a quick <strong>text word counter</strong> for a single paragraph or a
          full-featured <strong>free word counter online</strong> for exam preparation or
          professional writing, RealWordCounter has every feature you need — free, fast, and
          private.
          <a href="/word-counter">Open the word counter tool →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero .container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }

  .hero-heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .hero-accent {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 500px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .hero-cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .trust-badges {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .trust-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    padding: 5px var(--space-3);
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .trust-badge-green {
    background: var(--color-success-soft);
    border-color: rgba(22,163,74,0.2);
    color: var(--color-success);
  }

  .hero-page-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .hero-page-links a {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-body);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .hero-page-links a:hover { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; }

  .hero-page-sep { font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-mute); }

  /* Hero visual / mockup */
  .hero-visual { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; }

  .hero-card-mockup {
